<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Carlist War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1833–1840</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Carlist War (1833–1840) was a Spanish civil war over the succession to Ferdinand VII. Supporters of his brother Carlos, strongest in the Basque provinces, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a> and Catalonia, fought for him and for traditional rights against the liberal regency of Maria Christina for the young Isabella II. The Convention of Vergara ended the fighting in the north in 1839, and the last Carlist forces were defeated in 1840.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-carlist-war.jpg" alt="First Carlist War" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Lyde Hornbrook · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Puerta_de_Behobia_de_Irun,_bajo_el_ataque_de_las_fuerzas_Reales_Irlandesas,_el_17_de_mayo_de_1837.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
